# Files that are executed inside Linux containers, or shipped to a Linux host, must keep
# LF endings no matter what core.autocrlf is set to on the machine that checks them out.
#
# A CRLF docker-entrypoint.sh is fatal: the kernel resolves the interpreter as
# "/bin/sh\r", tini reports "exec ... failed: No such file or directory", and the
# container restart-loops with exit code 127 while the image itself looks correct.
# tools/hubctl and deploy/release/*.sh fail the same way once they reach a Linux host.
#
# Match Dockerfiles at ANY depth: the plugin images under packages/*/docker/ are built
# on a Linux host too, and a bare `Dockerfile` pattern only covers the repository root.
*.sh             text eol=lf
tools/hubctl     text eol=lf
Dockerfile       text eol=lf
**/Dockerfile    text eol=lf
deploy/ci/post-receive text eol=lf
*.py             text eol=lf
*.yaml           text eol=lf
*.yml            text eol=lf
# systemd parses units line by line; CRLF makes a directive value end in \r.
*.service        text eol=lf
*.timer          text eol=lf
